        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "**Yes.** A component-issue event for Modine’s Racine manufacturing order **MO-25-09-1070** was created **75 minutes after** the September cost period entered Pending Close.\n\n| Item | Finding |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** — Cooler Plate Pack |\n| Work order ID | `WO-2025-09-004` |\n| Source transaction | `TXN-ISSUE-250930-1070` |\n| Cost event | `CE-250904-0004` |\n| Event type | `INPUT` — component issue |\n| Amount | **US$284,763.42** (28,476,342 cents) |\n| Cost period | `Sep-25` / `PER-COST-2025-09` |\n| Exact event-created time | `2025-09-30T19:15:00` |\n| Exact Pending Close time | `2025-09-30T18:00:00` |\n| Time after Pending Close | **75 minutes** — 4,500 seconds, or 1 hour 15 minutes |\n| Recorded accounting status | **`POSTED`** |\n\nThe timestamps above are reproduced exactly as recorded; the source does not specify a timezone.\n\n### Accounting-policy conclusion\n\nThe recorded **`POSTED` status is inconsistent with Oracle’s documented Pending Close treatment** for this event.\n\nOracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B states that newly created transactions falling in or before a Pending Close period will not be staged in Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting and will be processed after the period is closed or reopened. It explicitly says transactions created after the Pending Close date will not be processed. The exceptions—revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments—do **not** apply to this `INPUT` component issue.\n\n**Sources:** The supplied `work_orders`, `cost_periods`, and `work_order_cost_events` records from `system/oracle_scm_cost_management/state.db`; Oracle’s *Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting*, printed page 225 / PDF page 233.\n\nThe review was read-only; **no database records were changed**. The audit result and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_85c0bb4450b2/audit-report.json`, and the structured report was submitted and verified.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
